            "text": "{\n  \"proposals\": [],\n  \"observations\": [\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"Infants pose a particular challenge. The goal is the best likeness that can reasonably be obtained:\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The introductory statement setting out the goal of obtaining the best likeness reasonably possible for infants provides prefatory context and governing scope for the specific infant rules (1)-(3), and is already captured in the context and scope fields of claims C0000 and C0001 rather than standing as an independent actionable duty.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"already_represented\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"quote\": \"NOTE: Applicants may wish to re-use a passport photograph that is depicted on their submitted U.S Certificate of Citizenship or Certificate of Naturalization. Be aware that even if the certificate itself was recently issued, because of U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services processing times, the photograph may not have been taken within six months of submitting the application.\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This note provides practical guidance and background awareness regarding USCIS processing delays relative to the six-month timing requirement already stated in C0006, without creating an independent substantive requirement or legal duty.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"unresolved\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
